  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a strong multimodal baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_009 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, weighted fusion) is chosen because: (1) multimodal is the most promising model setting for cellular profiling, combining complementary RNA and image signals; (2) scgpt is a learned biological encoder expected to outperform PCA at capturing cell-state structure; (3) resnet50 is a well-validated image encoder that is substantially cheaper than imagenet_vit_l, keeping the first experiment affordable; (4) singleprofile avoids aggregation overhead, isolating the core multimodal fusion signal; (5) weighted fusion is a standard, interpretable fusion strategy. This configuration sits in the moderate-cost tier—more expensive than unimodal or PCA-based configs but well below ViT-L + transformer-aggregation setups—leaving ample GPU budget for the remaining 9 experiments to explore multiprofile aggregation, ViT-L, and alternative fusion strategies. If it performs well, I can exploit by adding multiprofile/transformer/ViT-L; if it underperforms, I learn that the basic multimodal pairing needs rethinking before investing in more complex variants."
